{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/membership/Proofs.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T08:27:44.592049Z","id":"fd7c0d83818bd7436020b8ead16e31f237cc16b56a2f8e792ef8fc7bf2d9d37a","body":{"detail":"All nine QuorumIndex theorems in jarl/proofs/membership/project.json are execution, refinement or budget equations. The majority-support property exists only generically in Provium (provium/lean/Provium/NumericFolds.lean, Provium.OrderStatistics) and is never instantiated for Jarl. The consensus slice theorem JarlProofs.majority_position_in_bounds (jarl/proofs/consensus/Proofs.lean:81-93) proves only `index < total`. That bound still holds if `count - (count / 2 + 1)` is changed to `count - 1`, which would commit an entry replicated on a single voter. advance_commit (src/node.rs:1003-1016) relies on majority replication, yet coverage.json marks quorum_index as component_evidence, which invites the reading that quorum safety is covered.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1401},"end":{"line":1480},"content_hash":"066decd38ee2ddabda9a05269656f1a3e1e9110be8d2720d215c275d50b7a391"},"suggested_fix":"Add a Jarl obligation such as QuorumIndex.majority_supported: for deterministic callback replies f, a successful execution returning v implies `voters.length / 2 < (voters.filter (fun id => v <= f id)).length`, and the same for old voters when joint. Derive it from QuorumIndex.execution and Provium.OrderStatistics. Until then, state in README and PROGRESS that quorum_index has only execution and refinement contracts.","summary":"No Jarl obligation states the commit-safety meaning of quorum_index: that the returned index is matched by a strict majority of current voters and, when joint, of old voters","tags":["review","review:2026-10-07-deep","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"jarl/proofs/membership/Proofs.lean","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T10:08:39.037883Z","id":"c7b8e03ce2e48ba6b5069660996c1cfc5c7495d4ed3f68c46ce1798d93906d34","body":{"detail":"membership/project.json:444-476 lists 9 QuorumIndex.* theorems. membership/Proofs.lean:1401-1482 states them as equalities to numericRank, word/target/build refinements, response_budget and observation_complete. The rank-threshold lemmas (numericRank_threshold, provium/lean/Provium/NumericFolds.lean:43) are not instantiated in any Jarl proof. consensus/Proofs.lean:81-93 majority_position_in_bounds concludes only index < total, which `count - 1` also satisfies. coverage.json:4446 gives quorum_index status component_evidence.","kind":"comment","references":"fd7c0d83818bd7436020b8ead16e31f237cc16b56a2f8e792ef8fc7bf2d9d37a","summary":"confirmed: the nine QuorumIndex obligations are execution, refinement, budget and observation equations; none states majority support","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:a11d54e5-e61a-4ddb-ada4-de40e3db1dad"]}}
